      "t": "Mistral releases weights for its trillion-parameter AI model, targeting cybersecurity",
      "d": "Mistral says its new model can afford organizations a kind of control over its cyber defenses that closed models can't.",
      "u": "https://techcrunch.com/2026/10/29/mistral-releases-weights-for-its-trillion-parameter-ai-model-targeting-cybersecurity/",
      "m": "10. 29. PM 05:00",
      "ts": 1793293200000,
      "fullText": "French AI company Mistral has released the weights for its trillion-parameter open source AI model Mistral Large 4 (ML4), allowing businesses and governments to download and deploy the system themselves. Nicknamed &#8220;Le Chonk,&#8221; the model was first introduced earlier this month . The release comes as competition between open-weight AI developers like Mistral and closed-model providers like OpenAI and Anthropic heats up, with the former arguing that businesses and governments shouldn&#8217;t have to rely on outside AI companies for access to advanced capabilities. That argument may hold more weight in cybersecurity, where organizations want more control over their data and systems. Or, as Mistral&#8217;s CEO, Arthur Mensch, explained, AI should &#8220;be a tool for empowerment, not dominance.” With Chonk, Mistral doubles down on that position, arguing that it&#8217;s able to achieve &#8220;state-of-the-art performance&#8221; at a &#8220;fraction of the compute and capital committed by closed labs.&#8221; The release of the model&#8217;s weights — the numerical training that animates the system — ensures that other companies and government agencies will now be able to deploy ML4 for their own purposes. Mistral says that its model is comparable in terms of performance with a Chinese open-weight competitor, GLM-5.3, which was previously considered one of the best open-weight models in the world — particularly when it comes to cyber work. However, Mistral&#8217;s model uses 47 percent fewer tokens per task, making it significantly more economical than GLM-5.3. The company also claims that the model outranks all other open models when it comes to agentic coding tasks on Artificial Analysis’ Coding Agent Index, an AI benchmarking site. &#8220;Amid growing cyber threats, ML4 brings state-of-the-art sovereign cyber defense capabilities to enterprises and governments globally,&#8221; the company said Thursday. &#8220;Enterprise and public sector institutions can now "
